# nr-office-fonts: the new crate mixdog-fonts (font faces, system font discovery, CSS font matching, HarfBuzz-equal shaping, canvas measureText, font provisioning).

## native/core/Cargo.toml

[workspace] members: add, after "crates/mixdog-fsio" (any place in the list):

    "crates/mixdog-fonts",

[workspace.dependencies]: add, next to `mixdog-fsio = { path = "crates/mixdog-fsio" }`:

    mixdog-fonts = { path = "crates/mixdog-fonts" }

[workspace.dependencies]: add (owner decision "font parsing and shaping"; every crate below is in the local cargo cache; default
features of ttf-parser are kept: the crate reads variation axes and name strings, which need "variable-fonts" and "std"):

    ttf-parser = "=0.25.1"
    rustybuzz = "=0.20.1"
    unicode-script = "0.5"

unicode-script: the cache holds 0.5.9 (the plan said 0.5.7); rustybuzz needs >= 0.5.2, so one version serves both.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

New packages (all sources are in the cache; regenerate offline with `cargo update -w`, no other package changes):
  mixdog-fonts          deps: mixdog-fsio, mixdog-workspace-hack, rustybuzz, sha2, ttf-parser, unicode-script (dev: mixdog-office-base, serde_json)
  ttf-parser 0.25.1
  rustybuzz 0.20.1      deps: bitflags 2.x, bytemuck 1.x, core_maths 0.1.1, log, smallvec 1.x, ttf-parser, unicode-bidi-mirroring 0.4.0,
                        unicode-ccc 0.4.0, unicode-properties (already locked), unicode-script
  core_maths 0.1.1      dep: libm 0.2.x (cached 0.2.16)
  unicode-bidi-mirroring 0.4.0, unicode-ccc 0.4.0, unicode-script 0.5.9
rustybuzz's `wasm-shaper` feature (the only user of wasmi, which is not cached) is off by default and stays off.

