## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers no service.

## Consumers (later tasks)

The tasks that depend on this crate (the text-metrics port, the PDF font and embed tasks, the raster canvas) read these entry points:
  mixdog_fonts::css_font::parse(&str) -> Result<ParsedFont, FontError>           the ctx.font shorthand
  mixdog_fonts::measure::{measure_text, measure_parsed, faces_of}   measureText; the proof argument is a lane ReadProof
  mixdog_fonts::registry::Registry                            families(), family(name), register_file(proof, path, alias), register_dir(proof, dir)
  mixdog_fonts::discovery::{Catalog, scan, HostEnv}           the machine's fonts, scanned lazily once; Catalog::scan(proof, env) -> Arc<Scan>
  mixdog_fonts::provision::{NOTO_FONTS, FontDef, verify, installed_path, register_installed, mac_office_font_dir}
  mixdog_fonts::shape::{runs, hb_face, shape_run, shape}      rustybuzz shaping per script run
  mixdog_fonts::Face                                          names, style, metrics, axes, named instances, glyph coverage, load_all (ttc)

## Follow-up for the owner of native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/domain_seams/office_fonts.rs (not edited here)

That file holds its own copy of the pinned Noto table (FontDef, NOTO_FONTS, url(), verify). Once mixdog-fonts is a workspace member it can
depend on it (edge mixdog-app-server-daemon -> mixdog-fonts) and re-export mixdog_fonts::provision::{FontDef, NOTO_FONTS, verify}, keeping
only the download, the OS registration and the install steps; the table, its digests and the verify messages are the same text.

## Fixtures

native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json already carries the `office-measure` entry (this task edited it); the set lives in
native/core/fixtures/office-measure/ (golden.json, MANIFEST.json, faces/: three OFL Noto Sans faces and Miriam Libre, 245 KB). They are
not checked out in a sparse worktree: stage them with `git add --sparse`.

## Corrective batch 1: immutable snapshots and collection registration

register_bytes(path, Vec<u8>, family) -> Result<Vec<FaceId>, FontError> registers every member in index order,
sharing one Arc byte snapshot. Parsing is atomic before registry mutation. register_file/register_described keep
Result<FaceId, FontError> and return the first id after registering all members. register_dir returns newly added
face count, excluding duplicate registrations. Existing path/family/index registrations keep their original snapshot.
Pinned provisioning transfers verified bytes into register_bytes; it never reopens that file for shaping.
No workspace or consumer changes are included in this batch.

Phase 2 remains with the font implementation owner: variable coordinates in shaping and outlines, bidi and cluster
fallback, glyph offsets, synthetic styles and raster/hinting-compatible metrics, fontconfig and legacy cache contracts.
Phase 3 remains with the independent oracle/test owner: actual resolved-face evidence, all TextMetrics at task tolerance,
and deterministic isolated fixtures. Existing relaxed tests have NOT been tightened or claimed as parity evidence here.
The original @napi-rs/canvas/index.js guards automatic system/user loading with
`if (!process.env.DISABLE_SYSTEM_FONTS_LOAD)`. Set DISABLE_SYSTEM_FONTS_LOAD=1 BEFORE importing/requiring canvas in a
fresh recorder process, and remove the recorder's explicit installed-Noto/user-directory probing for an isolated oracle.
Only explicitly supplied fixture paths may be registered. This does not itself establish face-selection correctness.
Root compilation and independent review are still required; no build/test execution occurred in this batch.

## Verified provisioning collision correction

Private provision::register_verified verifies the incoming pinned buffer, then checks exact retained bytes for the
same registered family/path before any mutation. A different retained snapshot returns Provisioned::Rejected;
identical repeated verification is accepted. Old snapshots are preserved. General Registry APIs are unchanged.
Provision unit regressions exercise A-preloaded/B-verified collision and identical repeats with existing pinned
regular/bold fixture files only; registration_snapshot integration tests remain unchanged. No build or tests run.

## Root foundation integration

Workspace/dependency edges and isolated fixtures integrated. Unit and immutable
snapshot suites pass (41 tests), including verified-byte collision and atomic TTC
registration. Scoped all-target Clippy passes after lane-proof I/O in test helpers.
Historical twin_measure is intentionally not used as strict parity evidence: it
relaxes ink tolerances, skips cases and probes installed fonts. Those limitations
must be removed by the isolated strict phase2/3 corpus before product activation.
No measure consumer or font-install operation is activated here. Native-kernel
source/tool preparation remains pending the separately requested owner approval.
